tasks/BACKLOG.md:124:📖 **story-correctives-batch READY-FOR-GATES → ✅ SHIPPED ae0df5b06 (drained; see the SHIPPED row above) (branch `feat/story-correctives-batch`, base `e6c52b296`, 2026-09-07; Claude Opus 5 implementer on scratch `wt-story`, port 5303) — THE THREE BOSSES ANSWER THEIR OWN ACTS, THE ELEVEN SILENT PORTRAITS SPEAK, AND CHALK IS CANON ON BOTH SURFACES.** Owner: "fix these story parts please" (2026-09-06) and "yes, lets do 1, 2, and 3" (2026-09-07). **18 new beats, every one appended at the END of its chapter table so no in-file citation ABOVE that table moved (the ones BELOW it did, and all 31 were re-derived: see the re-base paragraph), every one carrying its `lore/STORYBOOK.md:NNN` citation in source, and NOT ONE existing beat re-keyed, re-copied or re-triggered.** **BOSS ACTS (7, F-SSG-5 / F-SS09-3 / F-SS10-1 / F-SS11-1 closed).** Every act the three boss systems report now reaches exactly one beat, proved act by act in the specs: THE CLAW (E8, not E5 — see F-STC-1) `e8-claw-paperwork` clerk (:505), `e8-claw-crown` prospector (:506), `e8-claw-winch` suit-fitter-e8 (:507), `e8-claw-anchor-feet` tavernkeeper (:508), matching `SalvageClawBossSystem.ts:236/:277/:301/:339`; THE DIGGER `e9-digger-boarding` prospector (:563) and `e9-digger-swap` canal-reeve-e9 (:564), matching `OldDiggerBossSystem.ts:267/:219` (`renovation` already had `e9-digger-correction`); THE QUIET `e10-quiet-approach` prospector (:612), matching `E10StaticBossSystem.ts:241` (`three-preserves` already had its beat). The acts are named for what happens and never renumbered to the book (F-SSG-6 holds). **THE ELEVEN SILENT FACES (11), each from a storybook line of its own, NONE left silent.** E2 on the Hill Mine unlock: `e2-tavern-welcome` tavernkeeper-e2 (:122 + :35, the wagon-ring intake form), `e2-boiler-fed-line` boilerwright-e2 (:105 + :109 + :77 — written to her TRADE only, because F-AGE-2 recorded that the plate is a woman while :91 implies a man; no line touches the wedding, so neither surface is contradicted), `e2-press-first-run` pressman-e2 (:93, "the Baron's rail brought the town its voice"), `e2-held-galley` typesetter-e2 (:85, Lan's own line kept verbatim: "It will keep. Truth keeps better than fear."). E3 on the return chain: `e3-lantern-walk-home` preacher-e3 (:143 THE RELAPSE + :148) — F-STC-4: the LINE is cited, the SPEAKER follows this file's own convention, because E3 names no preacher. E5 on the Deepwater unlock: `e5-cannery-hand-paper-boat` (:265 + :92, the paper boat at lunch, the E2 plant paid), `e5-shipwright-drydock` (:267 + :294), `e5-pearl-diver-ladder` (:267 + :248 + :295). E8 on the return chain: `e8-he3-assay-opens` he3-assayer-e8 (:486 + :512, keeping the E1 clerk's bargain, which is what a lineage is). E10: `e10-heir-always-said-so` eldest-heir-e10 (:584, his question as canon staged it, boarding KNOWING per ruling #7) and `e10-charter-keeper-first-charter` charter-keeper-e10 (:621 + :602). The two E10 portraits the ss-11 header called "a portrait waiting for a line" have one, and neither displaced the beat that blocked it. **CHALK (F-SS08-2 CLOSED).** `lore/STORYBOOK.md:421` PROPOSAL → CANON, with the date, the ruling (#13 of the twenty, owner 2026-07-18, already stamped at :739) and the wiki line that has carried the tag since (`lore/characters.md:14`). No other lore text changed. **THE COORDINATE RE-BASE, DONE RATHER THAN DISCOVERED LATER (F-GEN-1 / F-PORT-3 class).** Appending at a table's END protects every citation ABOVE that table, which is why it was done that way, but it still pushes everything BELOW it down, and a coordinate that cites an EARLIER chapter from a LATER header is exactly the class that rots. **31 in-file citations across 29 comment lines were re-derived by locating each symbol in the edited file, never by adding a shift to an inherited number, then verified 36/36 exact by a checker that rebuilds every range from the file itself** (the E3 note 430-431 -> 482-483, E3_STORY_BEATS 432-535 -> 484-607, E5 724-869 -> 796-981, E6 892-1015 -> 1004-1127, E8 1229-1404 -> 1341-1588, and thirteen beat ranges incl. `e8-riverward-launch` 1395-1403 -> 1507-1515, the e10-charter-press body citation for the third time). The E2 coordinates (380-427) are UNMOVED because the E2 append lands below all of them; the four RECORD paragraphs in the E10 header are untouched by design; the record of this re-base is appended at the FILE'S END, below every coordinate it describes, the technique the era-aging note proved. **EVIDENCE (measured on this tree, host shared with four other implementers).** `npx tsc --noEmit` clean · `npm run build` green (herald under ceiling) · `no-emdash-guard` 1/1 (289 tracked src TS files, 281 scanned) + `no-emdash-scan-space-guard` 8/8 · **all six touched chapter specs 58/58 on BOTH projects at one worker on port 5303, zero console/page errors**: `ss-03`+`ss-04` 12/12 (3.6 m), `ss-06`+`ss-09` 20/20 (7.0 m), `ss-10`+`ss-11` 26/26 (11.4 m) · 14 plain-boot 390 px screenshots in `reviews/shots-story-correctives-batch/` (560 KB, JPEG q60), one card per boss and one per face made to speak, taken INSIDE the town after Enter Town rather than over the menu (Mistake #10: where does the player see this) · tracked `reviews/shots-ss-*` churn restored with `git checkout --` before the commit. **OWED TO THE DRAIN: engine pin `cd7617b81dc0e6ac23bac08e13e535447f334eb0b5ba3fc09ce5544e25e62d33`** (era 5) — `src/story/**` is inside ENGINE_SOURCE_INPUTS, so `engine-era-guard` reds 1/5 naming exactly that hash and `assets/engine-era.json` is outside this task's firewall (F-2460-1 pattern: append the same-era pin AND the top-level `engineHash`). The full node-guard battery was deliberately NOT run (dispatch instruction); nothing is claimed for it. **FINDINGS (reported, not fixed).** **F-STC-1** the master's scope line says "the Claw (E5)"; the Salvage King's Claw is E8's boss (`lore/STORYBOOK.md:504-508`; `src/game/Game.ts:1112` binds `salvage-claw` beside the E8 path, and every existing Claw beat gates on `e8-mare-claim`), so its four act beats landed in `E8_STORY_BEATS` and `ss-09`. `ss-06` was still touched — for the three silent E5 faces, which is the other half of what E5 owed. **F-STC-2** `lore/STORYBOOK.md:466` (E7 chapter status) still reads "Chalk (PROPOSAL — first made citizen…)"; the firewall allowed only :421, so it is the last stale PROPOSAL tag for a character :739 already stamps CANON. One line, one drain. **F-STC-3** thirteen registered speakers outside this task's eleven still carry no beat, measured over `speakers.ts` against `beats.ts`: `kitchen-chemist-e6`, `appliance-wrangler-e6`, `diner-carhop-e6`, `depot-clerk-e6`, `playbook-librarian-e7`, `drone-keeper-e7`, `tape-courier-e7`, `combine-defector-e7`, `launch-master-e8`, `dome-gardener-e8`, `moon-born-child-e8`, `ice-quarry-chief-e9`, `weather-warden-e9`. Same shape of cure, one more batch. **F-STC-4** the `preacher-e3` assignment rests on this file's convention rather than a named E3 appearance; stated in the table's own comment rather than papered over. **F-STC-5** the storybook's Quiet Act 0 (the fading portrait) and Act 1 (the squalls) still have no state in any system, so `e10-portrait-fades` and `e10-unraveled-board` stay on the return chain; unchanged by this batch and re-recorded here so nobody reads the closed acts as all four.
