 the E5 switch one line above; the import gained one name. Tale/headline data lives in the same table as ordinary attributed beats, the shape ss-04 set (`beats.ts:409-410`). `artKey` set on the six beats whose plates exist on disk (`plate-contract-e8-mare-claim`, `-far-side`, `-low-orbit`, `-eclipse`, `plate-e8-boss-salvage-kings-claw`); no speaker added (F-SS09-1 below). EVIDENCE: `npx tsc --noEmit` clean · `npm run build` green (herald 1,158,214 B under the 1,500,000 B ceiling) · `e2e/ss-09-e8-beats.spec.ts` 6/6 desktop-chrome (2.4m) + 6/6 mobile-chrome 390px (2.4m), zero console/page errors, including three negative arms (E1's Claim, E3, and the three locked maps load no `e8-` beat before their own card unlocks) and an exact-order assertion on the six-beat arrival cluster · adjacent `ss-01`+`ss-02`+`ss-03`+`ss-04`+`ss-05`+`ss-06`+`ss-07`+`story-loop` on the final tree 30 passed / 3 failed on BOTH projects, and all three are F-2460-2's known pre-existing reds (`ss-01-beats.spec.ts:103`, `ss-03-beats.spec.ts:52`, `story-loop.spec.ts:185`), CONTROL-PROVEN this session on BOTH projects by reverting the slice's two src files to the lane base `eb7529a11` and reproducing the identical three at the identical lines (3 failed desktop, 3 failed mobile), then reapplying. ZERO caused here · the LEXICON pair `no-emdash-guard`+`no-emdash-scan-space-guard` 9/9 (285 tracked src TS files, 277 scanned, 8 skipped) · ENGINE HASH FOR THE PIN: `1052ba1ab016c53d1b6cceff3db4d0859b38ade38f7e07a95a51112ba3c51b81`, era 5, `engine-era-guard` 4/5 with the one expected red (`src/story/**` is inside ENGINE_SOURCE_INPUTS; the drain appends the same-era pin, F-2460-1's pattern). The full `test:node-guards` battery was deliberately NOT run (dispatch instruction, tonight's host load aborts it); nothing else is claimed for it · screenshots `reviews/shots-ss-09-e8-beats/` (8 files, 3.3 MB, scaled: desktop 900px wide, mobile 600px). **F-SS09-1 (non-blocking, reported not invented): Chapter E8 names five cast members with no registered speaker or portrait — the moon-born child, the dome gardener, the launch master, the suit fitter and the He-3 assayer (:485,:486). `src/story/speakers.ts:9-15` requires a processed portrait per speaker id; `assets/raw/` holds `tf-moon-born-child-e8.png`, `tf-dome-gardener-e8.png`, `tf-launch-master-e8.png` and `tf-suit-fitter-e8.png` but `assets/processed/` holds no `tf-*-e8` entry at all, so adding them would render a broken portrait. This table voices them through registered speakers and names them inside the lines, exactly as ss-06 and ss-07 did for E5 and E6. The cure is an extraction batch plus speakers.ts rows: an art task, not this one. The Household Law (`lore/canon-rules.md:19-20`) is honoured by keeping the moon-born child among the whole Canteen and its gardener, never alone.** **F-SS09-2 (FOR THE DRAIN, not a defect): the merged tree needs a FRESH engine hash, not the one above.** `1052ba1a…` was measured on this lane alone (base `eb7529a11` + the E8 table). RE-MEASURE `scripts/engine-era-guard.test.mjs` on the merged tree and pin THAT, updating both the appended pin and the top-level `engineHash` in `assets/engine-era.json` (F-2460-1: the append alone does not cure it). MERGE SHAPE, characterized rather than guessed: this lane's only `beats.ts` hunk is a pure APPEND at `@@ -959,6 +959,199 @@`, after `E6_STORY_BEATS` and before the trailing `STORY_RUNTIME_BEATS` export, and its only `StoryRuntime.ts` hunks are one import name and one switch line appended after the E5 line. `tasks/ss-08-e7-beats.md` is authored and `E7_STORY_BEATS` is absent from main at this base, so if the E7 lane lands first the resolution is the same pure UNION in era order (E7 then E8) at the same insertion point that ss-05/ss-06/ss-07 already proved, with no line of any table contested. **F-SS09-3 (engine gap, reported not fixed, firewall-respecting): the Claw's three acts cannot each own a beat, and a breach cannot fire one.** `src/game/Game.ts:5991` emits ONE `boss-arrival` per contract with no act or component discriminator, and `src/systems/SalvageClawBossSystem.ts` (which does track CROWN / WINCH / ANCHOR-FEET) emits no story signal at all — `grep -c emitStorySignal` returns 0 there, and 0 in `src/systems/E8SuitAirSystem.ts` and `src/systems/E8PhysicsSystem.ts` too. So STORYBOOK's four-act dread-to-landing choreography (:504-:508) is compressed into `e8-baron-at-the-pad` + `e8-salvage-kings-claw` on the single arrival signal plus `e8-claw-crew-walks` on defeat, and the era's signature mechanic (air as the wall, `:473`) gets its beat at contract-unlock rather than at a real breach. Nearest existing triggers were used and no signal was added, per the task's honesty guard. A `boss-act` signal plus a suit-air breach signal is the cure and it is an engine slice, not this one.
