acts/wire-crawler-3d/report.md`. 🚨 **F-RCA-1 (non-blocking, pre-existing, NOT re-recorded):** the crawler spec's `coldBaseline`/`mounted` drift UPWARD under host load on BOTH projects — 5 excursions against 31 clean observations, every one above load 14 and every one on a pin the dedupe never moved (390px `coldBaseline` 30 → 32, `mounted` 37 → 38 ×3; desktop `mounted` 37 → 38 at load 43.4). The railcar spec was exact in all 14 of its observations over the same load range — that is the control. A content-hash dedupe can only REMOVE textures, so this is not the atlas — it is the fixed 800 ms sample after the `frame > 12` gate (`wire-crawler-3d.spec.ts:118`), and `logs/suite-red-inventory-compact.json` (snapshot 2026-08-11, three weeks before the atlas merge) already carries the identical fingerprint at `renderer-count-artifact.ts:37` for both specs. Fix is spec-side (settle-condition sampling) and outside this task firewall. 🚨 **F-RCA-2 (non-blocking, tooling):** `artifacts/f1476-1/measure.mjs:21` — the measuring path the master cites — deletes the artifact before each run, which F-1478-1 turned into a required INPUT (`renderer-count-artifact.ts:29`), so it dies at `:33` with "renderer-count artifact missing" on run 1 (verified by running it; artifact restored byte-identical). `artifacts/s1477-noise/measure2.mjs:18` has the same defect plus a `gate-s1477` worktree that no longer exists.
