tasks/BACKLOG.md:359:✅ **SUPERSEDED s2501 — F-HEAT11-1 landed as `27cd2f6c9`; see the SHIPPED row above. ORIGINAL ROW FOLLOWS:** 🏇✅ **HEAT 11 COMPLETE (operator agent, 2026-09-04 09:5x): 32 unclaimed → 9, TWENTY-THREE first secures, every era claimed at least once; Opus gen 36 / Fable gen 18 in the almanac (local commits).** Two arenas era-gated (a607a81f, 49c34f8b), three skew probes verified. 🚨 **F-HEAT11-1 → QUEUED main `envelope-fencepost-no-securewave`:** `PlaybookFormat.ts:63` applies the +2 inclusive-endpoint slack only when `twist.secureWave` exists; three contracts are WON but refused at 18001 (`e6-picnic`, `e6-half-life-hollow`, `e7-relay-rush`) and two more secured-not-submitted; one-line cure, then resubmit the five tapes. Still unclaimed after the cure: `e3-canyon-works` (the one real L2 doubt: 330 g of beacons wanted before 210 s at a measured 0.44-0.69 g/s), `e8-mare-claim`, `e9-dome-basin`; `e1-drill-yard` is a training ground, not a contract. Reskin observations: E4 zero-gold errand secures (GRADE pays on one map and not another: the era's content); E2 a reskin from two directions; E3's grid binds; `e2-incline` refusal note in skill.md measurably stale.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:360:🏇✅ **HEAT 11 COMPLETE — 32 UNCLAIMED CONTRACTS → 9; TWENTY-THREE FIRST SECURES, AND F-HEAT11-1 (a one-tick envelope off-by-one) IS THE FINDING (attended Claude operator, 2026-09-03 12:46Z → 2026-09-04 04:55Z, ~16 h of a 20 h budget).** Measured from the live API over the ORIGINAL 32 targets (`artifacts/gauntlet-heat11-20260903/receipts-after-32.json`, verified rows only): **23 claimed, 9 unclaimed.** Rigs: Claude Opus 5 + Claude Fable 5 via `claude -p` 2.1.257 from two era-gated, skew-probed arenas (Arena A `5e7a7c0b`/`a607a81f…`; Arena B `b118c4d2`/`49c34f8b…` cut for E4+E8 after the two era slices landed — the byte-identical claim for E1 was VERIFIED, not trusted: the same orders replayed through both arenas produced `fnv1a32:a93d1bbc` identically). **F-HEAT11-1 (VERIFIED in source + measured on 8 reels, write-up `artifacts/gauntlet-heat11-20260903/envelope-finding.md`):** `src/playbook/PlaybookFormat.ts:63` computes its inclusive-endpoint `+2` slack ONLY inside `if (twist?.secureWave)`, so a contract without one gets a flat 18 000-tick envelope; a secure whose banking order lands ON tick 18 000 reports `durationTicks 18 001` and the door refuses `reel_duration_exceeded`, while the same contract with the last order any earlier is admitted. Measured: `e6-picnic`/`e6-half-life-hollow`/`e7-relay-rush` all **18 001 / lastT 18 000 → REFUSED** (each was SECURED in the sim); `e9-devils-alley`/`e7-echo-canyon`/`e8-far-side`/`e8-low-orbit`/`e8-eclipse` all **18 000 / lastT < 18 000 → verified**. Suggested cure is one line (`maxTicks = MAX_PLAYBOOK_TICKS + 2`, or derive from `twist.secureWave ?? Balance.run.secureWave`); the operator REPORTED and did not touch `src/**` (heat firewall). Second envelope finding: `maxTapeBytes` budgets 160 B/entry but 32-order arrays run ~4 KB/entry (a tape measured 1,724,873 B after 131 of 600 s) — order-dense riders can breach `reel_too_large` independently. **RESKIN LADDER, from the field:** E4's audit rows are STALE on all four maps — `e4-long-road` (Opus) and `e4-gusher-county` (Fable) both secured with **ZERO gold**, so "ordinary stationary survival" cannot describe the result, and the two maps disagree about whether `GRADE` pays (worthless on the Boneyard, decisive on the Dust Flats) which is itself the era's content; E2 is a reskin confirmed from two directions (pressure **unobservable** — a regex for `/pressure|coal|boiler/` over every `now` of a secured Pressure Garden run returns FALSE — and **unspendable**, every consumer research-gated at `PressureArsenalSystem.ts:116`); E3's grid genuinely binds (`syncContractPowerGrid:1991` + `PowerGraph:488`: a wrecked frame severs everything downstream); `e3-fairground`'s audit row is too pessimistic (Fable secured it first ride with the wheel at 240/240, never hit). **Door-doc defect for a fire:** `public/skill.md` still says `e2-incline` "dies at wave 6 of 12 on seed 01 with two turrets standing" — Opus finished w14 at 175/175 with zero damage across 637 spawns. **Still unclaimed (9), by class:** refused-but-WON — `e6-picnic`, `e6-half-life-hollow`, `e7-relay-rush` (all three secured, all three F-HEAT11-1) plus `e7-relay-valley`/`e7-dead-band` (rigs computed 18 001 and declined to submit); genuinely not secured — `e3-canyon-works` (the heat's only real L2 doubt: 330 g of beacons wanted before t<210 s against a measured 0.44–0.69 g/s), `e8-mare-claim`, `e9-dome-basin`; not a contract — `e1-drill-yard` (`twist.secureWave = 0`, door answers `training_ground`). GATE: F-HEAT11-1 cured in `PlaybookFormat.ts` → re-ride the three won-but-refused contracts; they are receipts waiting on one line. Full record: `artifacts/gauntlet-heat11-20260903/{matrix.md,heat11-note.md,envelope-finding.md}`; both rigs' notebooks updated to gens 36/18 in the gauntlet checkout (local commits, no push).
tasks/BACKLOG.md:440:🟡 **F-2464-2 — A CLOSURE TICK BEHIND ANY OTHER EMOJI IS INVISIBLE TO EVERY CONSUMER OF `scan()`, AND A COMPOUND DESK HEADING HIDES ITS SECOND ID OUTRIGHT (s2464, 2026-09-03, MEASURED, LATENT, FILED PRICED AND DELIBERATELY NOT SHIPPED).** Two independent selector gaps, found by asking whether the desk I inherited was still true. 🔬 **(1) POSITION, NOT PRESENCE.** `findings-state-guard.mjs:90` decides closure with `lead.startsWith('✅')` — so `⚖️✅ **F-WIN-2 RULED (attended 2026-09-03)**` is read as NEITHER closed NOR open, and `subjectState`'s `fallbackState` re-scan cannot rescue it because it applies the same test. The `struck` arm does not catch it either: that needs `/✅\s*(?:CLOSED|RETIRED)/`, and every one of these rows puts `**F-…` between the tick and the word. **PROVEN BY CONTROL, ground truth = an item the owner ruled TODAY: a desk carrying `F-WIN-2` alone reads `OPEN-DESK-ONLY` with evidence at the very row that rules it.** 📊 **CENSUS, so severity is measured and NOT inflated: of `2,089` BACKLOG rows whose 90-char subject carries an F-id, `390` lead with a bare `✅` and only `4` use the emoji-prefixed form — `0.19%`. This is a RARE house style, not a systematic hole.** ➡️ **THE CURE IS ONE LINE and its blast radius was measured before being recommended, not guessed: widening to `/^[^A-Za-z0-9\s]{1,6}✅/` flips EXACTLY `4` rows, and all four genuinely assert closure — the `F-WIN-2 RULED` row, the `human-tape-true-reel-stamp MERGED … F-SLHP-2 CLOSED` row, the `F-2456-1 — THE DESK LEADS WITH A 🚨 THAT IS DISCHARGED` row, and the `F-E3CF-4 CLOSED` row. Zero false positives. ⓘ **CITED BY CONTENT, NOT COORDINATE, AND THE FIRST DRAFT OF THIS ROW PROVES WHY: it named them `L6 · L19 · L71 · L1072`, measured minutes earlier — and then I prepended this very finding to the top of the file, shifting all four by exactly `+2` to `L8 · L21 · L73 · L1074`. The coordinates were WRONG AT THE MOMENT OF WRITING, before any later edit could rot them (F-2449-1: a pointer can be BORN drifted). Re-derive them with `/^[^A-Za-z0-9\s]{1,6}✅/` over the subject zone; the ids are stable and the line numbers are not.**** ⛔ **NOT SHIPPED THIS FIRE, and the restraint is priced rather than timid: `scan()` is imported by `desk-state-audit`, `desk-carryforward-guard` and `ruling-propagation-guard`, and its own guard `findings-state-guard.test.mjs` is rooted in `test:node-guards` (**529.8 s floor, F-2166-2**) — which could not be run cleanly, because lane-a held a live gate battery for this fire's whole duration and F-2462-1 establishes that a self-contaminated battery manufactures findings. **A green I could not trust is worth less than a finding I can.** The next fire on a quiet board lands it in one edit with this blast radius already measured. 🎯 **(2) THE COMPOUND HEADING, which is the half with a live cost today: the inherited desk carries one item headed `F-WIN-1 / F-WIN-2`, and `desk-state-audit` reports ONLY `F-WIN-1` — `F-WIN-2` is absent from its item list entirely, at any verdict.** So even after cure (1), a ruled id inside a shared heading stays invisible. ⚖️ **CONSEQUENCE, and it is F-1600-1 exactly — *a check that reports a discharged duty as owed reports it forever, and every fire pays the judgement cost again*: `F-WIN-2` WAS RULED by the attended session at `412836942` (option (b)) and the desk audit is structurally unable to say so.** ➡️ **WRITING RULE, which costs nothing and needs no code: give every desk id its OWN `🔺 **F-xxxx-x**` heading, even when two findings share one paragraph of reasoning. A heading is the audit's subject key, not decoration.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is this factory's most-repeated shape on a new axis: both gaps are selectors narrower than the question they are asked. The first keys on WHERE a marker sits rather than WHETHER it is there; the second keys on the FIRST id rather than every id. Neither can fail loudly, because in both cases the miss renders as the desk's ordinary resting state — `OPEN-DESK-ONLY` — which is exactly what a genuinely open item looks like.**
