tasks/BACKLOG.md:1296:🟡 **E2 COAL MOVES ONTO ITS OWN CLAIM, AND THE REASON THE OWNER NEVER FOUND IT (2026-08-21, headless Opus agent on `worktree-agent-a383c2ed5dd452ebd`, base `d775fca71`; PROPOSED, not yet drained).** TWO owner items in one slice. ⑴ **RULING** to the [F-E2PL-1] lever, verbatim **"sounds like a good idea"**: `coalSeams` is now a lawful twist key — added to `AUTHORED_TWIST_KEYS` with schema validation that refuses an empty list, a placeless seam, and coal on a contract declaring no `pressureEnabled` (nothing could burn it). `PressureSystem` reads `twist.coalSeams` and falls back to the exported `DEFAULT_COAL_SEAMS`; **both engines read it through one identical expression** (`Game.ts:1538`, `HeadlessContractSim.ts:821`). `e2-trestle` authors three seams along its mine spur (mean **29.4wu** from its stake) and `e2-incline` three in its lower yard (**28.8wu**), against the Hill Mine's measured **29.4** standard and the **55/58wu** they paid before. 📊 **THE LEVER WORKS — AND NEITHER MAP CONVERTS IT.** Pressure delivered DOUBLED (192→368 trestle, 192→384 incline; incline lance fires 164→288), the incline ceiling moved w9→w10, and across **96 runs on the new coal the only secure is still the run that DECLINES the line** (`dry-e2-trestle-02` w18 `bc515b13`). Both exemption rows STAY, reworded. 🔒 **ZERO-CHANGE PROVED TWICE:** `e2-hill-mine-01` reproduces `fnv1a32:c40556c0` after every edit, and all four dry controls reproduce their pre-ruling hashes **with the seam coordinates moved**; idle floors unchanged (w2/w1/w2/w2); audit summary unmoved at 468/1090/4, 6 exemptions. ⑵ **PLAYTEST REPORT** (owner, verbatim: *"I was not able to ever obtain coal or use the pressure weapons when I played maps in E2"*) — **INVESTIGATED, NOT ASSUMED. The coal was never buried:** every lump on all three maps measures **gap 0.000** against the sculpted ground, both viewports, and 0.8s standing on one yields its 4 coal. ⭐ **And the reason it escaped F-SEAM-1 is a real difference worth keeping: `GoldNode` places once at spawn and needed the `resampleVisualHeights` hook; `PressureSystem.syncSeams()` re-samples EVERY FRAME, so it is self-healing — its absence from that list is CORRECT and must not be "fixed"** ([F-E2CS-3], now a comment on the extended guard). 🎯 **WHAT ACTUALLY STOPPED HIM: the Hill Mine's briefing never mentioned coal.** It named the terraces, the switchbacks and the flooded gallery, while `e2-pressure-garden`'s card had said *"The coal seams cluster on the highest terrace above the boiler beds"* all along — one map in the epoch taught it, and the one he meets first did not. The coal is also **off-camera from the stake** (29wu north) and the lump reads as ambient scatter. ✅ **CURE SHIPPED — the missing sentence, in the house voice, on the three cards that lacked it**, pinned in `contract-briefings.spec.ts` so it cannot rot back out. Acceptance frames for the owner at `artifacts/e2-pressure-line/coal-shots/` (briefing → coal seen → coal cut, desktop + 390px). 🔺 Raises [F-E2CS-1] (the lump reads as scenery — OWNER: art brightening vs nerfing `coal_survey`), [F-E2CS-2] (the VIEW carries no coal — an agent cannot locate it through the public grammar; fire-authorable, the F-E3CF-5 shape), [F-E2CS-4] (**the trestle's only remaining lever is now [F-1608-2]** — 384 pressure and 46 shots reach the hpScale-30 railcar and it lives). Review `reviews/e2-coal-seams-and-legibility.md`.
