tasks/BACKLOG.md:1350:📮 **F-E2CS-2 AUTHORED + DISPATCHED s2142 → `tasks/fe2cs2-1-publish-coal-seams-on-the-view.md` (LANE-C; leaf `fe2cs2-1-publish-coal-seams-on-the-view` registered `queued` in the same commit) — THE COAL RULING TOLD THE PLAYER WHERE THE FUEL IS AND TOLD THE AGENT NOTHING.** 📐 **THE FINDING IS A DAY OLD AND IS THE REVIEW'S OWN:** `reviews/e2-coal-seams-and-legibility.md` (F-E2CS-2, shipped with `a7764dd6a`) — *"an agent cannot LOCATE the coal through the public grammar. The seam positions reach the prover only through `sim.pressure.diagnostics`; the VIEW carries no coal … **Fire-authorable**, and cheap."* **Verified at source by s2142 rather than inherited:** `grep -c coal src/agent/View.ts` → **0**, and `grep -n pressure src/agent/View.ts` → **0**. The view publishes GOLD seams **twice** — authored anchors on `stablePrefix.map.seams` (`:243`–`:247`) and live state on `now.seams` (`:321`–`:333`, which gained `x`/`z`/`anchorIndex` in the F-E3CF-5 cure merged `789dc39a7`) — and publishes coal **nowhere**. ⭐ **THE STABLE PREFIX, NOT `now`, AND THE REASON IS THE VOCABULARY'S OWN:** the coal review's PART 1 states *"the shape is deliberately `harvestAnchors`' own `{x, z}`: a seam is a place, not a machine"* — places live on `stablePrefix`, which is cached per run (`View.ts:169`, `:204`) and costs nothing per turn. **Seam depletion is deliberately OUT of scope** and the master orders that omission stated in the report so a later reader does not mistake it for an oversight. 🚫 **THE ONE TRAP DESIGNED OUT RATHER THAN DISCOVERED AT GATE TIME:** on a contract that declares no `pressureEnabled`, the master requires an **EMPTY array, not the default anchors** — the contract schema already refuses coal there *"since nothing could ever burn it"*, so publishing three fallback coordinates would tell a rider there is fuel on a claim that can never burn any. **A published lie is the exact class F-E2CS-2 belongs to**, and the cure must not commit it while curing it. Three test directions are required and the two load-bearing ones are the **authored** case (`e2-trestle`) and the **no-pressure** case — a defaults-only test passes just as happily if `twist.coalSeams` were ignored entirely. 🚨 **THE HASH CONTROL OUTRANKS THE FEATURE** (four captures across a declaring and a non-declaring contract, byte-identical): `f2138-1` ran the same control when it published `canyonConnect` and it came back clean — **which is a reason to EXPECT a clean result, not a reason to skip the measurement.** Any movement is a STOP and a finding, never a re-pin (F-1441-3). 🏷️ **NAMED `fe2cs2-1` DELIBERATELY, NOT `f2142-3`:** this fire had already spent `F-2142-1` and `F-2142-2` on unrelated findings, and F-2141-3 records precisely this collision shape — *"the id is minted from the task name by BOTH parties, at times neither can observe."* The master tells the runner in its header to file as `F-E2CS2-n` and never as `F-2142-anything`. ⓘ Firewalled off `PressureSystem.ts` (read and mirror its fallback rule, change nothing), off `assets/contracts/**` (the vocabulary shipped yesterday and is correct), and off `Game.ts` — **the browser legibility half is F-E2CS-1 and is an OWNER call** (brighten the lump, or a faint always-on ember tell, versus nerfing the `coal_survey` node). Drain owes the full ~405 s `test:node-guards` battery: this touches `src/**`. 🔴 **HELD s2143 — NOT MERGED, AND THE REASON IS BIGGER THAN THE SLICE (F-2143-3, BLOCKING; leaf flipped `blocked`/`gate-side`, corrective `fe2cs2-2-coal-seam-defaults-node-safe` AUTHORED + QUEUED to lane-c in this same commit under BUILD-ON-PREDECESSOR).** The feature is right and its guard is honest, but the import that delivers it — `View.ts` → `PressureSystem` → `Terrain.ts` → `assets/layer-contracts/m1-core.layer-contract.v1.json?raw` — drags a **Vite loader directive into the plain-node collection graph**, and under node it throws `needs an import attribute of "type: json"` during playwright's collection pass. 📊 **MEASURED BY ISOLATION, NOT ARGUED — one file reverted on the merged tree, everything else left merged:** with the slice's `View.ts`, `npx playwright test --list` returns **`Total: 0 tests in 0 files`**; with `View.ts` alone reverted, **`Total: 2958 tests in 425 files`**, rc 0, no TypeError. `View.ts` restored byte-identically after (SHA-256 `89d11a4f…6796`, by content compare). ⚠️ **THE SEVERITY IS THE FAILURE MODE, NOT THE COUNT: a suite that collects zero tests does not go RED, it goes EMPTY** — every playwright gate downstream of this merge would have passed by running nothing. That is Mistake #10 at the scale of the whole e2e surface, and `scripts/whole-suite-collection.test.mjs` exists for precisely it and caught it on the first battery. ✅ **THE RUNNER IS NOT AT FAULT AND THE DIVISION OF LABOUR WORKED:** its report says plainly *"Full `test:node-guards` remains owed by the drain, as required"*, and its own `tsc`/`build`/focused-test/`gate-caller-audit` greens are all real — none of them collect the playwright suite. 🧮 **FOUR REDS RESOLVED TO TWO SUBJECTS BEFORE ANY VERDICT WAS FORMED, WHICH IS THE REUSABLE HALF:** `whole-suite-collection`, its `cwd-invariance` sibling and `fixture-teardown` are **one defect wearing three names** (the latter two spawn the first as a child), while **`same-game report exemption reasons and citations match source` is INHERITED and NOT this slice's — it fails standing ALONE on main at `21425bf1d`** (`stale exemption reason for 'e2-incline' — regenerate with node scripts/same-game-audit.mjs --write-report`), arriving with the attended e5-stillwater admission whose regeneration was still in flight. **A failure COUNT invites a systemic story; the NAMES tell you two of the four were free.** 🔍 **F-2143-4 (non-blocking, inherited, deliberately NOT fixed here):** that stale generated report is whoever-next-touches-the-bench's, with the command the guard itself names; regenerating it inside an unrelated drain is how attribution gets lost. 🔍 **F-2143-5 (non-blocking, recurring):** the new guard constructs `HeadlessContractSim` with `admissionProbe: true` while the campaign harness — the consumer the field exists for — constructs it **without**. That is F-2141-2's shape recurring in the very next slice to ship a pinned view guard, one fire later; the corrective widens the guard by one no-probe arm rather than filing it again. 📌 **The `package.json` graft is SOLVED and recorded so nobody re-derives it:** main and lane each prepend exactly one new guard to `test:node-guards` (`campaign-harness-terrain` from this fire's f2142-1 merge, `coal-seams-on-the-view` from the lane); **keep both** — the two sides were proved byte-identical after stripping their respective prepends, and `merge-tree` confirms `package.json` is the ONLY conflicted path.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1352:📮 **F-2135-1 CENSUS ATTEMPT 3 AUTHORED + DISPATCHED s2141 → `tasks/f2141-1-canyon-census-run-3.md` (LANE-D; leaf `f2141-1-canyon-census-run-3` registered `queued` in the same commit) — THE THIRD ATTEMPT SHIPS ON A LEVER THAT WAS *MEASURED*, WHICH IS THE ONE THING BOTH PREDECESSORS LACKED.** ⚖️ **§7.5's changed-premise requirement is satisfied IN THE CODE, not in anyone's confidence:** attempt 1 (s2086) stopped because the harness could not select an E3 contract (cured by `--contract`, `ce75bc31970404a9a48c8e94a70c542739739112`); attempt 2 (s2135) stopped because its master's central lever named `HeadlessContractSim.ts:1837` — a real line inside `private diagnostics()`, the wrong object (F-2135-4) — cured by `f2138-1`, merged **`cd59fb273ed34a3905ac32bb9d4907322ad33109`**. 🧪 **THE AUTHORING FIRE RAN THE LEVER BEFORE WRITING IT DOWN (the /author-task §0.7 duty that F-2135-4 was born from ignoring), AND RAN IT AT THE CENSUS'S OWN PARAMETERISATION RATHER THAN ONLY THE TEST'S:** `sim.currentTurn().view.now.canyonConnect` returns `{"powered":0,"required":2,"byWave":6,"complete":false,"failed":false}` **PRESENT with `admissionProbe:true`, PRESENT with `admissionProbe` ABSENT, and PRESENT on the unreachable pinned seed `-02`** — three parameterisations, because the pinned guard `scripts/canyon-connect-view.test.mjs` ("Canyon Works alone publishes its live connection objective", 1/1 in 3.7 s) constructs with `admissionProbe:true` and **the census does not**, so a green there is not by itself a green here. The chain is closed by code as well as by measurement: `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts:1503` assigns `view.now.canyonConnect`, and `scripts/gr-sim-campaign.mjs:106` hands the player exactly `turn.view` from `sim.currentTurn()`. 🔓 **DISPATCHED OVER A HOLDING LANE, LAWFULLY — the F-2089-1 BUILD-ON-PREDECESSOR opt-in, used for what it was built for.** `lane/d` HOLDS 5 paths main has never seen (the proven epoch-3 checkpoint + the census player + attempt 2's artifacts); the usual SAFE-DUPE pre-flight would `reset --hard` over exactly the base this task must build on — Mistake #2 in its purest form. All 5 are declared `EXPECTED-HOLDS`, **measured live from `scripts/lane-usable.mjs lane-d` rather than remembered** (the opt-in's own stated requirement), and the runner's predicate was **simulated against the finished master before the `cp`**: token 1, declared 5, held 5, undeclared 0 → HONOURED. ✅ **AND THE MERGE THE PRE-FLIGHT DEPENDS ON WAS PROVEN CLEAN BEFORE DISPATCH, NOT ASSUMED:** `git merge-tree --write-tree main lane/d` → rc 0, tree `c242fc164ad1d81068d8d7f4c31fb266e812d2f1`, no conflict list; that tree was then read directly to confirm it carries **both** halves — the `:1503` publication AND all five banked files — so the master's Step 2 greps (each verified to return exactly 1 on a single line first, per F-1425-2) test a condition already known achievable. 🚫 **ONE HAZARD DESIGNED OUT RATHER THAN DISCOVERED AT GATE TIME:** the banked `census.json` carries `"status": "blocked"` with a `blockedReason` that is **now false**, and the player's `persist()` appends into whatever artifact it finds — so a naive re-run would publish a fresh census still labelled blocked. Scope 1 orders it **moved** to `attempt-2-blocked/`, never deleted (Retention Law). ⚠️ **WHAT THE MASTER REFUSES TO OVERCLAIM, stated because attempt 2 died of exactly this: the census player has NEVER EXECUTED PAST TURN 1.** Its six-site route, harvest/poll fallback and pair-buying logic are banked, not proved. The firewall therefore carries an explicit 🔓 LIFT on that one file under three binding limits — every change reported with its reason, nothing touching the objective/deadline/seed/contract/harness, and no invented routing policy to manufacture a number — with Law 2 restated: if the honest route cannot be flown, **STOP**. 📐 **GATE B and GATE C are unchanged and both are restated in the master as EXPECTED rather than as blockers:** `gr-sim-campaign.mjs:113` throws `ended unsecured at wave N` above any leg-artifact write, so on the expected NO the player's own per-turn trace is the only survivor; and `:93` reads `benchSeeds[contract.id]?.[0]`, so the two-seed census remains **unsatisfiable through the sanctioned instrument** and must be reported as not-established rather than quietly reported as one seed. ⓘ The `f2135-1-canyon-census-run` leaf stays `stopped` — its stop is retained evidence, and it is retired as `superseded` in the SAME commit as attempt 3's merge, never before it (drain-block-check's own standing instruction).
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1373:🔴 **F-2135-4 (s2135 2026-08-21 — MY OWN LEVER CLAIM WAS OVERSTATED AND THE RUN STOPPED ON IT WITHIN FOUR MINUTES. THE VIEW CARRIES `canyonConnect` *CONDITIONALLY*, AND I ASSERTED IT UNCONDITIONALLY AFTER READING THE ASSIGNMENT BUT NOT THE SPREAD.)** 📋 **WHAT HAPPENED:** `f2135-1-canyon-census-run` dispatched to lane-d at 17:22:05 and took a lawful **Law-2 STOP** at 143,088 tokens — `stopped-s2135-law2-view-drops-canyon-connect-…`, run log `tasks/runs/20260821-172205-lane-d-f2135-1-canyon-census-run.md.log`. Its words: *"Harness stopped before the leg ran: `Error: Canyon connect diagnostics were absent from THE VIEW.`"* **Zero damage, nothing merged, firewall held, typecheck/build/unchanged-contract checks all passed.** 🔍 **RE-VERIFIED AT SOURCE BY ME RATHER THAN INHERITED, AND THE RUNNER IS RIGHT.** I cited `HeadlessContractSim.ts:1837` — which is only the *assignment* `const canyonConnect = this.canyonConnectDiagnostics();`. **The field reaches the view at `:1871` through a CONDITIONAL spread — `...(canyonConnect ? { canyonConnect } : {})` — and `canyonConnectDiagnostics()` returns `null` at `:1993` whenever `!grid?.connect || !this.powerGraph`.** So the key is **absent from the view on every turn where the power graph is not yet built**, including the first view a player is handed. The identical conditional spread governs the terminal `outcome()` at `:1211`. ⚠️ **THE CLASS, AND IT IS ONE THIS FIRE HAD ALREADY WRITTEN DOWN TWICE THAT DAY: I read the line that COMPUTES a value and asserted the line that PUBLISHES it.** F-2135-1 and F-2135-2 were both found by reading publication sites carefully (`:113` throwing above the artifact write; `:93` indexing seed zero) — and then the same fire asserted a third publication site from its assignment alone. **"The value is computed" and "the value is on the wire" are two facts, and only the second is what a consumer can rely on.** ✅ **WHAT THE RUN NEVERTHELESS PROVED, and it is the expensive half of the task: THE CHECKPOINT WORKS.** The runner built a genuine epoch-3 profile — *"Checkpoint lawfully activated E1 → E2 → E3 via `activateEpoch`; no unlock bypass"* — completing each predecessor megaproject through `MEGAPROJECT_STATE_KEY` and packing with `packActiveProfile`. **GATE A is therefore CONFIRMED, not merely reasoned: `epochIsActive('epoch-3-voltage')` is the whole gate, and `--resume` can supply it.** F-2135-2's one-seed constraint also re-confirmed by the run. ➡️ **OWED — attempt 3, and §7.5 is satisfied because the premise changes again:** the census player must treat an absent `canyonConnect` as *"the power graph is not built yet"* and record the trace from the turns that DO carry it, rather than guarding on first-view presence. **Before authoring, establish one fact this fire did not: whether `this.powerGraph` is ever non-null for `e3-canyon-works`, and from which turn** — if it is never built, the trace lever is unavailable and F-2135-1 has no cure short of an instrument change, which is a different and larger task. **Re-use the runner's checkpoint script; it is proven work.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1375:🔬 **F-2135-1 + F-2135-2 (s2135 2026-08-21, FIRE-AUTHORED + DISPATCHED — THE CENSUS GATE WAS DECLARED OPEN FOUR FIRES AGO AND THREE MORE GATES STOOD BEHIND IT; THE SANCTIONED HARNESS CAN ONLY PUBLISH A *POSITIVE* CENSUS, AND THE ONE ANSWER THIS CENSUS EXPECTS IS NEGATIVE.)** 📋 **THE INHERITED CLAIM, RE-VERIFIED RATHER THAN CARRIED.** `reviews/f2120-1-campaign-harness-contract-select.md` closes *"E3+ census slices become fire-authorable"* and F-2086-1's standing `GATE: an E3+ census slice is not authorable until the harness can select its contract.` is genuinely **OPEN** — the `--contract` cure is live at `scripts/gr-sim-campaign.mjs:64-75`/`:201`/`:205` (merged s2122 `ce75bc31970404a9a48c8e94a70c542739739112`). ✅ **AND IT REFUSES LOUDLY EXACTLY AS DESIGNED — PROVEN BY RUNNING IT, NOT BY READING IT:** `node scripts/gr-sim-campaign.mjs --player scripts/f2086-canyon-census-player.mjs --contract e3-canyon-works …` exits 1 with **`Contract "e3-canyon-works" is locked: The Voltage Age awaits — raise the Dynamo Hall.`** (`FakeStorage` is in-memory, `:24-26`, so the probe mutated nothing on disk). ⚠️ **GATE A — THAT MESSAGE IS FLAVOUR TEXT AND A READER WILL TAKE IT FOR A BUILD REQUIREMENT.** `src/meta/ContractUnlock.ts:22` gates on `epochIsActive(epoch.id)` **alone**; the sentence is assembled at `:28` from the *predecessor* epoch's `megaproject.raiseActionText`. This contract's own row is `"unlock": "default"` (`assets/contracts/epoch-3-voltage/contracts.json`), so `:35` returns unlocked the moment the epoch is active. **`epochIsActive('epoch-3-voltage')` is the ONLY gate on `e3-canyon-works` — no secured predecessor, no science, no Dynamo Hall** — which both confirms the f2120-1 drain's source-read YES and strengthens it from *"the pointer transfers"* to *"the pointer is the whole gate."* 🚨 **F-2135-1 — THE HARNESS CAN ONLY REPORT A YES, AND THIS CENSUS EXPECTS A NO.** `scripts/gr-sim-campaign.mjs:113` throws `ended unsecured at wave N` **above** every leg-artifact write, and securing is itself gated on the very objective under measurement: `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts:1695` computes `objectiveAllowsSecure = (!this.manifest.twist.powerGrid?.connect || this.canyonConnectCompletedByDeadline)`. **So if the wave-6 deadline is missed — precisely what F-E2S-4's 2.77 s result predicts — the sanctioned instrument yields no rows, no `eventLogHash` and no margin, only an exception.** This is F-2086-1's class one level in: that finding was *the harness cannot select the contract*; this one is *the harness cannot express the answer*. 🚨 **F-2135-2 — AND IT RUNS ONE SEED.** `:93` reads `benchSeeds[contract.id]?.[0]`, index zero always, while `assets/contracts/bench-seeds.json` pins **two** for this contract (`-01`, `-02`). The predecessor master's *"at least 2 seeds, 2 runs each"* is **structurally unsatisfiable** through the campaign harness, so any census run here reports one seed or admits why it cannot. ✅ **THE LEVER THAT DEFEATS BOTH, PROVED BEFORE AUTHORING (§0.7): the player module already sees what the census needs.** `HeadlessContractSim.ts:1837` puts `canyonConnect` — `{ powered, required, byWave, complete, failed }`, declared `:1991` — on the **turn view** handed to the player every turn, and `:1175` puts the same block on the terminal `outcome()`. **So the player records the whole margin trace itself, the number survives the throw, and no sanctioned script is edited.** 📮 **AUTHORED + DISPATCHED to LANE-D: `tasks/f2135-1-canyon-census-run.md`** (leaf `f2135-1-canyon-census-run` registered `queued` in the same commit). It is **attempt 2** under a genuinely changed premise (§7.5), and it orders the predecessor's already-drained answers **CITED, not re-derived** — `required: 2` counts powered `consumer`/`gallery` nodes, six beacons, **330 g**, `byWave` compares the wave index — because re-deriving merged work is Mistake #8's shape. Scope: a genuine epoch-3 checkpoint via `activateEpoch` in the `src/meta/DebugEraSeed.ts:15-16` pattern (**no unlock bypass, no `assets/` edit**), a trace-recording player, the run through the **sanctioned** harness, and a report that states the margin whichever way it falls. Firewalled off **all `src/**`**, **all `assets/**`** (the deadline and the seeds are the SUBJECT), and **every existing `scripts/*` file** including the retained `f2086-canyon-census-player.mjs`. ⓘ **The owner's deferral still governs the RULING** (verbatim *"I never played that level ever, I can't really decide on that"*, with the standing permission that *"a fire MAY run the census MEASUREMENT"*): this produces a number, takes no fork, and recommends no balance change.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1413:🔵 **F-2127-2 (s2127 2026-08-21, advisory, non-blocking — the new seam assertion is CORRECT but cannot say WHAT broke).** `e2e/agent-view.spec.ts:557-559` ("the seeded rider view stays cache-shaped and grows one honest wave at a time") collapses to `expect(views.wave3.now.seams.every(...)).toBe(true)`, so a failure reports only *"expected false to be true"* — naming neither the seam nor which of `x`/`z`/`anchorIndex` went wrong, against a six-seam fixture. That is a diagnosability cost on a guard whose whole purpose is catching a subtle join bug; a per-seam loop would fail loudly. **Tests the right thing in both directions, which is what the master asked for** — worth a cheap follow-up, not a block. *(Spotted independently by s2126 before it died mid-gate; re-verified at source here.)* ⏩ **TAKEN s2133 → `tasks/f2133-1-seam-legibility.md` (lane-d, queued, leaf registered)**, paired in one master with **F-E3CF-5’s owed "+ audit rows" half** because they are literally the same predicate asked twice: the e2e arm (`active ? finite x/z && anchorIndex >= 0 : all null`) is exactly the contract the audit row must publish. Re-verified at source by the s2133 author, not inherited: the collapsed `.every(...)` is live in `e2e/agent-view.spec.ts:512` ("the seeded rider view stays cache-shaped and grows one honest wave at a time"), and `grep -c seam scripts/same-game-audit.mjs` returns **0** on main. ✅ **Lever proved BEFORE authoring (§0.7): `same-game-audit.mjs:30` already SSR-loads `HeadlessContractSim`**, so the audit can read a real view — the row extends an instrument that already has the capability rather than assuming one. Scope is diagnosability ONLY (the predicate semantics are firewalled), scope 2 requires a manufactured-defect proof that the new message NAMES the seam, and scope 4 caps the added audit cost at ~15 s with an explicit narrowing STOP.
