# Boss fidelity depends on large forms and surface mapping

Review of current base d41ab98ce on sol/boss-art-fidelity-review found seven authored machine GLBs, but only six are referenced by runtime. Land Yacht still uses raw plate component crops. Dredge Queen and Salvage Claw use the adopted detail-opus5 GLBs; the base and Sol alternatives are archived assets, not the current comparison target.

Fresh imports/renders of all seven plus five runtime captures of Queen, Homemaker and Claw confirmed scope. Strongest shape opportunities: Homemaker rounded appliance body/apron/vacuum, Claw suspended crescent grapples and hanging underside, Old Digger industrial superstructure and deep bucket wheels. Shared generated atlases preserve palette and line rhythm rather than semantic panel placement. Several runtime systems alias albedo into strong full-surface emission, so material and geometry issues must be reviewed separately.

No assets or production code were changed. The proposed first pilot is Homemaker, preserving its three component meshes and chair state. All current GLB loaders pin exact triangles and named morphs; future replacements need those contracts retained or deliberately updated. Echo and Quiet are procedural encounter effects, and Baron has a sprite body; they are not missing equivalent machine GLBs.

